.TH CB_FREE_NODE 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
cb_free_node \- Free memory allocated for a Critbit tree node

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/cb_internal.h>

.IB void
.IB cb_free_node (
.IB void* ptr
.IB );

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBcb_free_node\fR function frees the memory allocated for a Critbit tree node. It recursively frees all child nodes before freeing the current node itself.

The function takes one argument:
.TP
.IR ptr (void*)
A pointer to the node to be freed.

The function does not return any value.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBcb_free_node\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/cb_internal.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    struct critbit_node* node = (struct critbit_node*)malloc(sizeof(struct critbit_node));
    if (!node) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Failed to allocate memory\n");
        return 1;
    }

    // Assume the node is initialized and has children

    cb_free_node(node);

    return 0;
}
.nef